# Template — `infra/deploy.sh` substitutes {{DOMAIN}} and installs this at
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile. Not consumed directly.
#
# Caddy handles the Let's Encrypt certificate and renewal automatically; the
# only job here is reverse-proxying to the API process on localhost. Caddy
# forwards X-Forwarded-For/Proto by default — nothing extra to configure.
#
# The Host header is rewritten to `localhost` before proxying upstream:
# the API's own Host-allowlist (apps/api/src/http/app.ts, `allowedHosts`)
# only trusts its own bind address, as a DNS-rebinding defence — it never
# heard of the public domain, and shouldn't need to. That's safe to do
# here because Caddy is the only way in; the API port isn't reachable from
# outside this box at all (not in the security group).

{{DOMAIN}} {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4319 {
		header_up Host localhost
	}
}
